  "description": "New York's 25th Congressional District, covering all of Monroe County and parts of Ontario County, is a safely Democratic seat (Cook PVI D+10). Incumbent Rep. Joseph Morelle (D), first elected in 2018 after the death of Rep. Louise Slaughter, is seeking a fifth full term. He faces two Democratic primary challengers — former Greece School Board member Sherita Traywick and former Brighton Town Board member Robin Wilt, who previously ran against Morelle in 2018 and 2020. The Republican nominee is Monroe County Legislator Virginia McIntyre, and independent candidate Kloud Walton is also on the general election ballot. Key issues include immigration enforcement, affordability, and the Trump administration's policies.",
